{"header":{"deal":"Multi-channel retailer with 120 stores","ae":"Tom","acv":null,"outcome":"Lost","scope":null,"competitor":"Adyen","incumbent":null,"tag":"Support and service","runner_up":"In-store and online together","tag_why":"The deal turned at the store ops workshop. When Bev asked who does the installs, our answer was a partner and we had nobody who had run a store rollout, while Adyen arrived with a retail team that had done store rollouts and offered one contract."},
 "sections":{
  "trigger":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E1","excerpt":"Returns. Last holiday season. Buy online, return in store.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E2","excerpt":"The store couldn't see the online order, so staff were refunding to gift cards or telling people to mail it back.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E3","excerpt":"they'd just launched a loyalty program that was supposed to work everywhere and didn't, because store and web were two different customer records.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E4","excerpt":"Their COO, Angela, apparently stood in a store on December 27th watching the returns queue. That's the story everybody there tells.","label":"opinion"}],"insight":"This evaluation started as a store operations problem: returns at the till and split customer records. It was never a web checkout problem. The origin story inside the company centers on the COO in a store, not the CTO, which pointed to who would own the decision long before the signature did.","messaging":"Lead retail pitches with the cross-channel return and the single customer record (buy online, return at the till, loyalty that works everywhere), not with checkout conversion."},
  "decider":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E5","excerpt":"The CTO, Raj. He ran the RFP, he was my contact the whole way.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E23","excerpt":"Angela's team. Stores.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E24","excerpt":"Angela.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E26","excerpt":"Once. The kickoff.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"Angela signed with Adyen, and her team asked for the store workshop. Yet the rep first named Raj as the decider, because Raj ran the RFP and was his contact. We sold to the process owner and met the person who signed once, at the kickoff. Raj's support for us rests only on what he told the rep, and it is unclear how much weight his view carried.","messaging":"When the trigger is operational pain, aim retail messaging and proof at the COO and store operations as the economic buyer, not only at the CTO who runs the RFP."},
  "competitor":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E6","excerpt":"This is secondhand. Raj told me afterwards.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E7","excerpt":"they came in with a retail team, people who'd done store rollouts, and they talked about one platform for the tills and the website, on one contract.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E8","excerpt":"And they named retailers Angela knew.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E11","excerpt":"Raj forwarded me a list of 14 questions and 11 of them were about stores.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"By Raj's account, Adyen pitched people, peers and accountability: rollout veterans, retailers Angela knew, and one contract. That is a direct answer to Angela's fear of two vendors pointing at each other. After they met Adyen, 11 of the customer's 14 questions were about stores, so the evaluation moved away from the web ground we were winning. Everything about Adyen's pitch reached us only through Raj, after the decision.","messaging":"Counter 'one platform, one contract' with a named retail rollout team and peer retailer references, rather than restating the platform claim."},
  "message":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E13","excerpt":"Reaction: the online checkout demo. Their ecommerce lead loved it.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E15","excerpt":"Online and in-store on one platform, the line between them has pretty much disappeared.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E16","excerpt":"that's a diagram.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E17","excerpt":"Then she asked how a return works. Step by step. At the till.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"M3 failed with exactly the audience it is meant for. Bev, the head of store operations, dismissed it as a diagram and immediately asked for the operational steps, which the rep could only describe. The part that landed, the checkout demo, impressed the ecommerce lead, who was not the person who signed.","messaging":"Replace the M3 line in store-led deals with a step-by-step, live walkthrough of an online order returned at a till."},
  "decided":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E19","excerpt":"Nobody on our side had run a store rollout.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E20","excerpt":"When Bev asked who does the installs, I said we'd bring in a partner. She wrote something down and didn't ask another question.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E21","excerpt":"I knew on the drive home.","label":"opinion"},{"id":"E22","excerpt":"Right before that, honestly, we were ahead. Raj said so. We'd won the web side.","label":"opinion"}],"insight":"The rep felt the deal was lost at the workshop. The customer brought six store operations people; we brought an AE and a solutions engineer, and our answer on installs was a third party. To a COO who doesn't want two vendors pointing at each other, that partner answer may have recreated the exact problem, though why Bev stopped asking questions is not established. Being 'ahead' was Raj's view, and Raj was not the signer.","messaging":"State plainly who owns installs and store rollout end to end, and if partners are involved, position us as the single accountable party."},
  "gaps":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E28","excerpt":"can I talk to them?","label":"quote"},{"id":"E29","excerpt":"we couldn't set up a call in time.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E30","excerpt":"Then a rollout plan. Dates, who installs, what happens to the old tills.","label":"fact"},{"id":"E31","excerpt":"They wanted to watch an online order get returned at a store till, live. We described it. We never showed it.","label":"fact"}],"insight":"The customer asked us for three proofs: a retailer to call, a rollout plan, and a live return at the till. We delivered none of them; we sent a case study and gave descriptions instead. M8's 'see our customer stories' is the wrong format for this buyer, because Angela wanted a conversation with a peer. It is unclear whether the live return demo was missing because of the product or because of preparation.","messaging":"For store deals, back M8 with a reference call that can be arranged quickly and a live cross-channel return demo, plus a template rollout plan (dates, installer, old-till handling)."},
  "language":{"covered":true,"evidence":[{"id":"E32","excerpt":"One system for the tills and the website.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E33","excerpt":"I don't want two vendors pointing at each other.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E34","excerpt":"one customer, one basket.","label":"quote"},{"id":"E35","excerpt":"They never said 'unified commerce.' We kept saying 'in-person payments' and 'point of sale.' They said 'the tills.'","label":"fact"}],"insight":"The customer described outcomes and accountability: one system, one customer, one basket, no vendor finger-pointing. We described categories: unified commerce, in-person payments, point of sale. Bev repeated 'One system for the tills and the website' every time, and we never adopted it.","messaging":"Use 'the tills', 'one customer, one basket' and single-vendor accountability in retail copy instead of 'unified commerce' and 'point of sale'."}
 },
 "close":{"gaps":[
  {"question":"What was the deal size (ACV)?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Tom what ACV was proposed, and whether Raj ever shared Adyen's commercial terms."},
  {"question":"Who made the final call, and how do you know?","kind":"dodged","follow_up":"Ask Tom, and Raj if he is reachable, what role Raj's recommendation played in Angela's decision and whether Angela ever saw our final proposal."},
  {"question":"What did they use before (incumbent)?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Tom which payment and till provider the customer used before the RFP."},
  {"question":"Did the web business also go to Adyen, or only stores?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Tom whether any part of the business (for example online checkout) stayed open to us."},
  {"question":"Why couldn't we show a live till return or arrange a reference call in time?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask the solutions engineer whether a live online-to-till return demo exists, and ask Tom what blocked the reference call."},
  {"question":"How did we answer the store questions (wifi drops, rollout, Saturday till outages)?","kind":"skipped","follow_up":"Ask Tom for our written replies to Raj's 14 questions."}
 ],"rep_takeaway":"When the pain started in the stores, the store side holds the pen, whoever runs the RFP. Get in front of the signer more than once, bring people who have done store rollouts to a store workshop, and when a buyer asks to see something, show it live instead of describing it."},
 "confidence":"medium"}
